@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Read-only reference use — browse, inspect and hand off without mutation
start
:Open public workspace;
switch (Chosen page)
case (Collection)
  :GET /api/dataset;\nsearch supplied text and metadata;\nkeep collection review status visible;
case (Dictionary)
  :GET /api/dictionary;\nsearch source-labelled senses;\npage matching results;
case (Synthetic examples)
  :GET /api/examples;\nshow constructed=true provenance;\npage practice examples;
endswitch
:Inspect the original text, glosses\nand available source context;
if (Copy to Franc Analyzer?) then (yes)
  :Pass text unchanged through openCompiler() in App.tsx;\nlabel Collection/reference/synthetic origin;
  :Show the draft in Franc Analyzer;\nno test is saved until Analyze is selected;
else (no)
  :Keep browsing without a save;
endif
if (Request an existing recorded reading?) then (yes)
  :POST /api/readings/lookup\nwith text, language, Origin and CSRF;
  if (A reading exists?) then (yes)
    :Play or download its existing audio;\nshow browser playback errors honestly;
  else (no)
    :Show unavailable recording;\nno synthesis or upload fallback;
  endif
endif
stop
legend bottom
  The sources are separate datasets, not subclasses of one collected-statement entity.
  Human collection place/date/consent are unconfirmed; a label or review flag is not fieldwork certification.
  No Collection, grammar or audio editing occurs; browsing and handoff never add an entry or a test.
endlegend
@enduml
